+Zstd creates its shared wave control before the checkpoint but does not fork
+workers until checkpoint restore returns. This avoids restoring a process wave
+while workers are blocked on a shared spin barrier. The post-restore worker
+topology and the 64 KiB per-worker warmup preceding `WORKBEGIN` are unchanged.
+
 The Graph500 binary is built with `-march=x86-64`, not `x86-64-v3`, because the
 same binary must execute on the host CPU through KVM and on gem5 O3.
